{
  "title": "ISic000693. Epitaph for Tullia Symbiosis",
  "body": "<div id=\"editions\"><div class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Alex Antoniou, Jonathan Prag; edition source: autopsy Prag 2022-07-14, in the Antiquarium, room 5, case 5, third shelf.</div><div id=\"edition-interpretive\" lang=\"la\">  <div class=\"textpart\" lang=\"la\"><span class=\"ab\" id=\"div-interpretive\">  <a id=\"al1-interpretive\"><!--0--></a><span class=\"linenumber\">1</span><span data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Tullia\n                    Symbio\n                    sis\"><span data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Tullia\">Tullia</span>  <br id=\"al2-interpretive\"><span class=\"linenumber\">2</span><span data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Symbio\n                    sis\">Symbio-<br id=\"al3-interpretive\"><span class=\"linenumber\">3</span>sis</span></span> vix(it) ❦ ann(is) ❦ <br id=\"al4-interpretive\"><span class=\"linenumber\">4</span>VII </span></div>  <p class=\"miniapp\"></p></div><div class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Alex Antoniou, Jonathan Prag; edition source: autopsy Prag 2022-07-14, in the Antiquarium, room 5, case 5, third shelf.</div><div id=\"edition-diplomatic\" lang=\"la\"><div class=\"textpart\" lang=\"la\"><span class=\"ab\" id=\"div-diplomatic\"><a id=\"al1-diplomatic\"><!--0--></a><span class=\"linenumber\">1</span><span data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Tullia\n                    Symbio\n                    sis\"><span data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Tullia\">TULLIA</span><br id=\"al2-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">2</span><span data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Symbio\n                    sis\">SYMBIO<br id=\"al3-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">3</span>SIS</span></span>VIX❦ANN❦<br id=\"al4-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">4</span>VII</span></div><p class=\"miniapp\"></p></div></div>  <div id=\"facsimile-images\"><h2>Facsimile Images</h2><a href=\"ISic000693_tiled.tif\"><img title=\"I.Sicily with the permission of the Assessorato Regionale dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana - Dipartimento dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana; photo J. Prag 2022-07-14\" src=\"ISic000693_tiled-thumb.tif\"></a><a href=\"ISic000693.jpg\"><img title=\"I.Sicily with the permission of the Assessorato Regionale dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana - Dipartimento dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana; photo J. Prag 2022-07-14\" src=\"ISic000693-thumb.jpg\"></a><a href=\"ISic000693_right_tiled.tif\"><img title=\"I.Sicily with the permission of the Assessorato Regionale dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana - Dipartimento dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana; photo J. Prag 2022-07-14\" src=\"ISic000693_right_tiled-thumb.tif\"></a><a href=\"ISic000693_right.jpg\"><img title=\"I.Sicily with the permission of the Assessorato Regionale dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana - Dipartimento dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana; photo J. Prag 2022-07-14\" src=\"ISic000693_right-thumb.jpg\"></a></div>  <div id=\"apparatus\"><h4>Apparatus criticus</h4><ul><li><span><span>Text from autopsy</span></span></li></ul></div>  <div id=\"translation\"><h2>English translation</h2><p class=\"translation-author\"><a href=\"http://orcid.org/0000-0001-7077-0703\">Alex Antoniou</a></p>  <p>Tullia Symbiosis lived for 7 years</p>  </div>  <div id=\"commentary\"><h2>commentary</h2>  <p>As Fasolo notes, Symbiosis as a personal name (as opposed to the use of the adjective or verb to describe a partner) is extremely rare.</p>  </div>  <div id=\"bibliography\"><h2>bibliography</h2>  <ul><li> 1989.0338m <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001283\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001283</a></li><li> Manganaro 1989 165 no.21 fig.21 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001831\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001831</a></li><li> Fasolo 2013 84 no.32 fig.58 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002011\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002011</a></li></ul>  <ul><li></li></ul>  </div>  <div id=\"handnote\"><p>A moderately deep v-cut, with wide modules in lines 1-2, narrower in line 3. Letters have pronounced but simple wedge serifs, and pronounced curvature on Y and X. The interpuncts in line 3 (only) have the form of hederae.</p> Line 1  50  Line 2  44-46 (Y=50)  Line 3  37-45  Line 4  30  Interlineation line 1 to 2    </div><div id=\"license\"> Licensed under a Creative Commons-Attribution 4.0 licence. </div>",
